---
module: spec_tree
func_id: collect-linked-resources
---

***conformance tests***

# stops-at-the-func-id
A tree has the functionalities f1 to f4; each fi links `ri.md`, its conformance scenario links `ci.md` and its acceptance scenario links `ai.md`, each link with its target as text.
- Collecting with scenarios up to f2 returns true and the registry targets are `a2.md`, `c2.md`, `r1.md`, `r2.md`.

# every-functionality-and-scenario
Collecting the same tree with scenarios and without a func-id returns false and the registry targets are `a1.md` to `a4.md`, `c1.md` to `c4.md` and `r1.md` to `r4.md`, sorted.

# without-scenarios
Collecting the same tree without scenarios gives the registry targets `r1.md`, `r2.md`, `r3.md`, `r4.md`.

# same-link-twice-records-both-sections
A tree whose `implementation reqs` item and functionality both link text `notes` to `notes.md` gives one registry entry with sections [`implementation reqs`, `functional specs`].

***acceptance tests***

# tree-is-not-a-mapping
Collecting from a list instead of a tree raises `plain_source_tree must be a dictionary.`.

# unknown-func-id
Collecting the tree of f1 to f4 up to f9 raises `frid f9 does not exist.`.

# same-text-other-target
A tree whose two items link the text `notes` to `a.md` and to `b.md` raises `The file b.md is linked to multiple linked resources with the same text: notes`.
